dpapp@amisk.cs.ualberta.ca (Denis R. Papp) writes:

> Ok I can only manage to get those annoying |- characters for nethack
>on the unix - if I log in remotely then I can get solid lines and color
>(IBMgraphics and color) but spaces appear as you move around.

>Anyways, how do I go about getting good graphics (or font) for nethack?
>ie. what do I put in the .nethackrc, anywhere?


Assuming that you have a PC, you can run chrhack, the graphical extension
for Nethack on PC's.  You need to set the IBMgraphics and color options
to true.

	To use the graphics:

		1) run the version of chrhack appropriate to the version
		   of nethack you have.  (there's and older version in
		   volume18 of the cpib archives on ftp.ulowell.edu)

		2) run your terminal program.  I assume that you would
		   need a dos based program - I haven't tried it with
    		   windoze...  As long as the text font remains changed,
		   it should work on the host machine.

		3) log on and play nethack - remember to set the IBMgraphics
		   and color options for maximum effect. 

		    
	
